description:
FILED s478 (Fable, 2026-09-08) from the s473c review probes.  PRE-EXISTING: identical on main c709804a and on the s473c MERGE-READY tree 472f17c8, under default and under PCL_OPT=line-track.  docs/not-supported.md "`$SIG{__DIE__}` and `$SIG{__WARN__}` handler invocation" blesses it ("requires CL condition restarts and is deferred") but names no owner; this task is the owner (the standing rule: a not-supported entry names its owner).

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 vs PCL):
  $SIG{__DIE__} = sub { print "H: $_[0]" };
  eval { die "e1\n" };          print "1: $@";
  my $z = 0; eval { 1/$z };     print "2: $@";
  eval { my $u; $u->m };        print "3: $@";
perl prints an `H: ...` line BEFORE each of 1/2/3 (the handler sees the message the die will carry, incl. the ` at FILE line N.` suffix for the runtime-raised ones); PCL prints none.  `$SIG{__WARN__}` DOES fire (#1223 fixed its re-entry).

SHAPE OF THE FIX (not designed): the handler runs INSIDE the die, before unwinding (perl calls it with the message, and the handler may itself die with a different message, which then becomes the exception -- the Carp-in-handler idiom); so it is a hook at the ONE raise site (`p-die` + every runtime `error` that becomes a perl die), keyed on the `%SIG` entry, with perl's re-entry rule (`$SIG{__DIE__}` is localised to undef WHILE the handler runs -- `perldoc -f die`).  Measure the cost on the die path only; the non-die path must not pay.  Affected: perl-tests/die.t rows commented out (not-supported entry) -- un-comment them with the fix and edit the baselines row by row.

=== DONE (s497b) ===
$SIG{__DIE__} is called at the ONE raise site of every perl-level die: %p-die-error (every string die â p-die's and the runtime's own fatals) and p-die's object branch, BEFORE unwinding, inside eval too; $_[0] is what $@ will hold (%p-die-text, shared with %p-caught-perl-value) or the reference itself; a handler that dies replaces the exception; no re-entry (*p-in-die-handler*, the __WARN__ shape); a code ref or a sub NAME is called, DEFAULT/IGNORE/""/undef are none.  The reproducer prints perl's lines (location text aside, #1595).  everyday programs/nested-eval-errors now `same`.  perl-tests/die.t handler rows restored (OK 3/0 -> 7/0); companion op/die.t 9/11 -> 19/7.  ir-spec Â§6.3c.  Residue: a string eval's COMPILE error does not call the handler -> #2409.
